    "note": "For the transverse and oblique archetypes the CAD-side rule substitutes the slab's thin axis at min_dot 0.7 and drops the walls (apps/testlab/main.cpp:1865-1875), while the mesh-side selector honours normal_min_dot = -1 literally and keeps every in-box face (main.cpp:937-975). The traction is then rescaled onto the smaller CAD area, so the resultant stays correct while the distribution smears onto the walls. A thin slab is what prevents that; a normal filter cannot, because the filter is relative to the traction, which is transverse in those cases and can never select an axial annulus."
